# Round-3 housekeeping (narrowed in round 4, F-173). Proving a fix in
# apps/web/scripts/assert-no-inlined-secrets.mjs sometimes needs a real Next.js build with a
# temporary component or route reading an env var, always deleted immediately after each
# proof, but this backstops that manual cleanup in case a step is interrupted mid-round, so a
# probe file can never be swept into a commit by an unrelated `git add`.
#
# F-173: the original `app/probe-*` pattern would have silently swallowed a future real
# liveness/uptime route named `apps/web/app/probe-*`, which would 404 in production with no
# diff to look at, and any ignore pattern here also blinds `git status --porcelain` to that
# file class, which is why the orchestrator's cleanliness evidence now uses
# `git status --porcelain --ignored`. `tk004-scratch-probe-*` is namespaced to this TASK's id
# specifically so no plausible product route or component name ever collides with it.
_tk004-scratch-probe-*
# Route-handler probes can't use a leading underscore: Next.js treats a leading-underscore
# folder as a private, non-routed folder, which would make the probe route unreachable and
# defeat the point of proving it. Same namespaced prefix, without the underscore.
app/tk004-scratch-probe-*
